        and the equipment types that we target generally will not warrant a large
        residual position. We anticipate that approximately 25% to 35% of our
        leases will be operating leases under which the rental payments we receive
        will return approximately 80% to 85% of the purchase price we paid for
        the equipment. Thus, based on the past experience of its senior management
        team, our general partner believes that both the number of our leases
        and their estimated residual values which might entail aggressive residual
        positions will not be material based on our total equipment investments.
        We plan to realize residual income on our operating leases using the following
        four methods:</font></p>
